[size=5][b]The Courier's Ledger[/b][/size]
[i]Everyone you have met, where they are now, what they teach and what they sell.[/i]

Ever needed that one trainer whose name you have forgotten, or wondered which merchant had the robe with Fortify Alteration? The Courier's Ledger keeps track for you. It is a helper, not a cheat: nobody is teleported and nothing can be taken.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Everyone you have talked to.[/b] The game already remembers who has spoken with you, so the ledger fills itself, also in an existing save.
[*][b]Quest targets.[/b] People that a running quest points at are listed too, in yellow, with the quest's name.
[*][b]Find a name fast.[/b] Alphabetical list with tabs (All, A-F, G-L, M-R, S-Z) and a name search.
[*][b]Colour by role.[/b] [color=#fff266]Quest target[/color], [color=#73bfff]trainer[/color], [color=#ffd159]merchant[/color], [color=#d199ff]fence[/color], [color=#ff994d]innkeeper[/color], [color=#80e680]follower[/color], [color=#ff8cbf]can marry[/color], [color=#8c8c8c]dead[/color]. Each role has its own filter.
[*][b]Details.[/b] Where the person is now, what and how high they train, what they trade in and when, how they feel about you, and how far away they are when they are near.
[*][b]Inventory and stock, look only.[/b] See what a person carries and what a merchant sells, including the effects of enchanted items, potions and scrolls. Ingredients are shown without effects: those are yours to discover.
[*][b]Find Item.[/b] Search by name or by effect ("robe", "alteration", "fortify smithing") across the stock of the merchants you know and, if you like, people's inventories.
[*][b]Track on map.[/b] One click puts a quest marker on the person: on the map, on the compass and above their head, also through walls and floors. While you track someone, other quests' markers are hidden so yours stands out. They come back when you stop tracking.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/30379]SKSE64[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/120352]SKSE Menu Framework[/url] (version 3)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Tested on Skyrim SE 1.6.1170. Built for 1.5.97 and 1.6 with CommonLibSSE-NG, but only 1.6.1170 has been tested in game.
[*]VR is not supported.
[*]Light plugin (ESPFE). Safe to add mid-game.
[*]Names are read from the base record, so name mods work and nothing hooks the name functions.
[*]No scripts run in the background. The quest only exists to carry the tracking marker.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Use[/b][/size]
Open the SKSE Menu Framework menu and pick [b]The Courier's Ledger[/b]. There are two pages: [b]People[/b] and [b]Find Item[/b].

[size=4][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]
If you are tracking someone, press [b]Stop tracking[/b] first so the other quests' markers come back. Then save and remove the mod.

